th as  he's visibly beat down from this  experience it crushed me a little bit  watching her tend to him while he makes  the decision to lie to her about what  happened well this is a betrayal of  their honesty policy it felt more like  watching a person trying to buy just a  little more time to think their way  through an impossible mess of  inevitabilities he knows Kim has met  Lalo but he still wants to find a way  that it doesn't mean that she's in the  game he lays down the law and says he  can't have her involved with Lalo that  he's worried about her  and that the only thing that kept him  going out there was knowing that she was  there waiting at home she agrees to stay  away from Lalo and asked him if all of  what he went through was worth it he  responds to by telling her to go look  inside the bag there she finds the  $10,000 stacks of money that he earned  for his trouble but she also sees the  second best lawyer mug with a bullet  hole in it this is proof that Jimmy  isn't telling her the whole story but  she doesn't bring it up in that moment I  assume she knows that he's gonna need  some time to recover from this trauma  and probably hopes that he'll eventually  come clean when he's ready as viewers we  have no idea how they'll come out of the  other side of this but we can see that  their love and care for each other is  real the shot of Kim's eye through the  bullet hole in the mug is a nice touch  as she starts to see just how dangerous  everything is around Jimmy at this  moment Kim plans to stay home and  support Jimmy in his recovery but it  turns out he's in no shape to sit still  we learned that he's also in no shape to  tell the truth about what happened when  Kim gives him the perfect opportunity  instead he pretends to get honest  telling her that he had to drink his own  pee like that was the worst thing that  happened while he was gone this was the  saddest part of the episode for me it  just lays everything that's tragic about  their relationship bare kim looks inward  to find the right way to give Jimmy the  opportunity to unburden himself she's  thoughtful and she does it from a place  of care he isn't able to do it and  that's completely understandable on some  level but to watch him pull some saw  like maneuver out at this moment it's  just really difficult to watch after  that we learn he's also in no shape to  be in court  we don't witness what happens in the  courtroom but a DA bills description of  Jimmy snatching defeat from the jaws of  victory is probably all we need to know  from there we make our way into Mike's  car where he delivers one of his classic  speeches where he distills things down  in a way that's level-headed and clear  but in a real way comforting in the  moment of delivery his point is there  will come a day when he will realize a  day has gone by where he hasn't thought  about being out in a desert and what  happened when he realizes he's capable  of that he'll know he's capable of  continuing to forget in other words  we'll take time and he's speaking from  experience and he's not wrong about that  the other point he makes is that people  don't randomly end up wandering through  the desert with 7 million dollars cash  after surviving a shootout choices Mike  and Jimmy made put them there and he  makes a fair point that in the case with  the bandits it was us or them they were  in the game Jimmy's having a hard time  processing he brings up Fred from travel  wire and voices his concerns for doing  all this that they're doing just to get  Lalo out of trouble  Mike agrees with him that there are  problems with the situation with Fred in  hints that getting Lalo out is only part  of a bigger picture he stops short of  telling Jimmy what the plan is but  perhaps this makes things a little  easier to swallow  either way Mike's age advice is the kind  of thing that takes some time to digest  and we'll see later that Jimmy is still  trying to work his way through it Kim  tries to throw herself into the office  and throw herself back into her work but  it becomes clear that almost losing  Jimmy has put things into perspective  for her as she tries to dictate a letter  a framed thank-you note and photo of one  of her pro bono cases catches her eye  before we can even figure out what's  happening she quits the firm and makes  her way out the front door after  grabbing the tequila bottle top that her  and Jimmy scam Ken winds into buying for  them on some level Kim has been  dissatisfied with her job which is  boring and unfulfilled she's made an  attempt to balance that out by doing the  pro bono cases and it's clear here that  she just can't continue doing it at the  same time she's giving up a lot of  security that this job provides a career  that she built through her own hard work  and this is something that will come  back to Mike seems to be functioning at  a much higher level than Saul as we  watch him report in to Gus from the  tattoo on the bandits we learned that  they were Colombians this convinces Gus  that they were hired by Juan balsa but  he doesn't really explain the motives  other than saying he thought he was  protecting their business Mike is on his  way out but stops to tell Gus there's  one more thing for a second I worried  that he was gonna bring up Jimmy and Kim  but instead he tried to get Gus to let  nacho go he points out that they won't  need him anymore that he's basically  served his purpose but Gus isn't moved  he compares not  to a dog that has bitten every owner  it's had and tells Mike that requires a  firm hand or for the dog to be put down  Mike doesn't like Gus's reasoning and he  definitely doesn't like that he  threatens nachos father to control him  by fear but he sees he isn't gonna win  the argument with his boss on his way  out of town Lalo goes to visit Hector at  Casa tranquila the situation the  Salamanca's find themselves in is not  ideal but Lalo tries to spin it in the  best way he can he will have the ear of  Don Eladio when he goes south and he's  confident that he can turn him against  Gus  we learned that Tuco is supposed to get  out of jail in 11 months so nacho won't  have to run their operations for very  long he says he knows Tuco can be  difficult when he's on the stuff but  he'll make sure that he stays clean once  he gets out he tells Hector that family  is everything  and it sort of brings the feels because  you can see that Lalo feels bad about  leaving his uncle alone as he walks out  the door we get this sad shot of Hector  with this party hat on and we wonder if  he's thinking that this is the last time  he's going to see Lalo alive nacho  drives although out to the well where  Jimmy met the cousins he tells them that  he can leave but at the very last second  he knocks on the window and gets back in  the car he didn't see Jimmy's car on the  way in and he can't leave before he  investigates they backtrack and they  find the esteem in the ditch where Mike  and Jimmy left it and after he jumps  down to take a closer look he notices  the bullet hole in the door this  confirms there's more to the story than  what Saul told him and he tells nacho to  take him back to Albuquerque  Kim returns home and delivers the news  that she quits Schweikart and Cokely  Jimmy doesn't take it well and he tells  her that he thinks she's making a bad  choice he tries to tailor Mike's  monologue about choices to the situation  but does a terrible job of it Kim pleads  her case effectively and makes the point  that it's her decision and besides Jimmy  isn't really in a position to question  anyone about their choices before they  can work things out Jimmy gets an urgent  phone call from Mike just as someone's  knocking on their front door Mike tells  him to keep the phone on but hide it so  he can hear what's happening inside the  apartment we learned that it's Lalo at  the door and he invites himself in he  manages to be completely menacing and  still slightly charming  at the same time he wants to hear about  what happened in the desert and when  Jimmy repeats his story Lalo wants to  hear it again this apartment scene is  long intense but somehow it manages to  fly right by Lalo is obviously trying to  catch Jimmy in the lie and he seems  content to wait as long as necessary we  watched as Jimmy's nervousness is just  ratcheting up with each retelling it's  getting worse and he begs for Lalo to  let him leave  Mike enters the scene looking at Lalo  through the scope of a sniper rifle he  has a clear shot but it's not clear to  us whether he's there to take that or if  he's just there to find out if Jimmy's  gonna break and give Lalo information  sensing that this is what is probably  going to happen Kim steps up and lays  into Lalo even though she's probably  terrified of Lalo she acts tough and  pokes holes and each concern he brings  up she effectively turns things around  saying that if Saul Goodman is the only  person you can trust with your money  you've got real problem there's no  decisive victory here it's just enough  to push Lalo back on his heels and get  him to leave the apartment the only  thing that's actually decided here is  that if Kim wasn't in the game before  she definitely is now and that's where  we leave things Lalo isn't done but he  goes to the car and tells nacho they're  headed to Mexico Mike can leave  reporting back that's all stuck to the  story  Jimmy is all sorts of messed up but for  now he's safe and so is Kim but they're  firmly in the game with one Episode to  go so it was a really good setup for the  finale I like the way they took the time  to do what they needed to do with Jimmy  going through what he's going through  and how all of that came down through  Kim it's a tense place that we find  ourselves in Kim's situation feels more  desperate and dangerous than it ever has  and we're seeing a vision of Jimmy where  he may be more broken than he's ever  been before it was a well-c