lbuquerque  she stepped in to go toe to toe with  Lalo and that might be something she  learned before she went to law school  it's a little frightening that the  teaser was a mirror of something stupid  that showed them living separate lives  before coming back together at the end  of that season if this shows them  wanting to come together does that mean  that it's before they go off to live  separate lives I mean we know this is  probably coming but with each episode it  somehow gets harder to accept one last  thing Kim quitting her job wasn't  completely out of nowhere but it does  have a big impact on the future of how  the show is structured Kim has existed  on the legal side with the cartel world  with Mike and Gus being in the other  side with Schweikart and Cokely in the  rearview mirror everything in the story  including all the characters exists on  just one side  only one side in the coming weeks let's  discuss how that will change as we  approach the end of the series going  through season six so I still have a lot  on my mind but I'm gonna end it there  let's talk in the comments about where  we think things are going let me know  what you thought about this episode what  do you think it means about the finale  check out the video I made the other day  about Kim's fate it talks about the  possible outcomes based on what we know  from Breaking Bad and other things we've  learned along the way please like this  video if you enjoyed it please subscribe  to my channel if you haven't already  thanks for watching I will talk to you  soon
 

